{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 6f8ae7847f5e4fbde92eaf81c1abee55ad8be68d on planner/docs-paths-c1-20261110, all 10 artifacts, for item C1 of documentation request 044311b0, request e59d46d0, under promise b1390427 and review request df6b4ad5. `docs/mcp.md` is now the agent reference. `docs/hosted-mcp.md` holds the operator's hosted endpoint and metrics, and a note keeps the measured figures. The moved words are unchanged, and every section that a test reads is byte for byte the same.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- The tests' text. `describe.test.ts`, `inventory.test.ts`, `counter.scope.test.ts`, `lending.scope.test.ts` and `recipes.scope.test.ts` read `docs/mcp.md`. Lines 1 to 1847 are identical at main a419407e and at the head except two links, at lines 82 and 136, which now point to `hosted-mcp.md`. Those lines hold every worked example and tool section. The sections \"The W1 inventory\", \"Taking part in a Counter\" and \"Taking part in the lending library\" are byte-identical up to their next `## ` heading. The heading after \"The W1 inventory\" is still \"The hosted endpoint\", so the inventory slice is unchanged.\n- The words. `docs/mcp.md` loses 758 lines. All but five reappear verbatim in `docs/hosted-mcp.md` or the figures note. The five are three lines with rewritten links, the \"Hosted framing figures\" heading, which moves up one level, and the old source line. The added lines are links, headings, the source stamps, the introduction of each new page, the hosted endpoint stub and the new \"Response limits\" section. `hosted-mcp.md` says that this revision did not compare the moved text with source.\n- Response limits. The 4 KiB, 8 KiB and 64 KiB bounds match `BOUNDS` in `packages/mcp/src/service.ts:146`. The 256 KiB page of `tools/list` matches `service.ts:86` and `:395`. \"No cap applies to the whole list\" repeats the old page.\n- The links. On my own extracted copy of the head, `check-doc-links.mjs` checks 1,226 local links and finds none broken